  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodeEscape.Programming.QuestionData
  id: PY_RUN_08_DATA_TYPES
  language: 1
  topic: Data Types
  difficulty: 0
  questionType: 2
  questionText: The variable text holds a number written as text. Fill in the blank
    to turn it into a whole number, so adding 3 works.
  code: 'number = ____

    print(number + 3)'
  answerFormat: 2
  choices: []
  correctChoiceIndex: 0
  monospaceChoices: 0
  acceptedAnswers: []
  caseSensitive: 1
  referenceFill: int(text)
  runTests:
  - setup: text = "7"
    expectedOutput: 10
  - setup: text = "12"
    expectedOutput: 15
  - setup: text = "0"
    expectedOutput: 3
  effectId: counter
  explanation: Text and numbers are different data types. int() converts text such
    as "7" into the whole number 7, so number + 3 can be calculated.
  hint: A built-in function turns text into a whole number. Its name is the data
    type it makes.
  wrongChoiceFeedback: []
  wrongAnswerFeedback: Use the function that converts to a whole number, and put
    the variable text inside its brackets.
